  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nPrincipal (P) = ₹8000\n\nRate (r) = 5% p.a.\n\nTime (t) = 2 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nA = P(1+(r)/(100))^t\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nA = 8000(1+(5)/(100))²\n\n⇒ A = 8000(1+(5)/(100))²\n\n⇒ A = 8000(1+0.05)²\n\n⇒ A = 8000(1.05)²\n\n⇒ A = 8000(1.1025)\n\n⇒ A = 8000 × 1.1025\n\n⇒ A = 8820\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (2).**\n\ndd",
